    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn data sufficiency for number puzzles.\n\nHere the first question is not always 'What is the number?'\nIt is often 'Do I have enough information to determine what is asked?'\n\nWe will test each statement before combining them.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "In data sufficiency, the target comes first.\n\nDo not immediately combine every statement.\n\nAsk: what exactly must be known? A whole number? A ratio? A difference?\nThen test Statement I alone and Statement II alone before using them together.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
